#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:37
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A sibling session (any coding agent) has a PR whose full tier is green as judged and wants it merged. It does not yet know whether a merge manager is active."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:85
#. Diagram label
msgid "Acknowledged in time?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:72
#. Diagram label
msgid "Announce and note the merge manager"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:19
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Any coding agent with a PR ready to merge. It first checks whether a merge manager is active; if none is and one is needed, it elects one with its siblings by the fixed rule; a lone or lapsed session manages its own PRs. It never merges another session's PR, never pushes to another session's branch, and treats a merge manager that does not acknowledge within the stall window as stalled."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:59
#. Diagram label
msgid "Elect the merge manager with the siblings"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:66
#. Diagram label
msgid "Elected this session?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:106
#. Diagram label
msgid "Lane handed over or lapsed"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:40
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge manager active?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:54
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge manager for its own PRs"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge manager needed?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:101
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge manager watch"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:13
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge request: find or elect the merge manager"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:114
#. Diagram label
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "No merge manager is needed (a lone session, or a lapsed lane): the session is its own merge manager for its own PRs only, so it runs the merge manager loop for them. It does not announce itself to the others; it posts the six lines in its own chat and asks the owner by card."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:109
#. Diagram label
msgid "Own PRs landed"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:36
#. Diagram label
msgid "PR ready to merge"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:73
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Send \"merge manager: <session id>\" to every sibling and the owner, and note it durably on the coordination work item, so it is used by all, including siblings started later."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:78
#. Diagram label
msgid "Send the six-line merge request"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:18
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sibling session"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:92
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled-agent triage"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:93
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tell the owner that the merge manager stalled, then re-elect with the stalled session excluded. The new holder announces itself, takes over the queue and tells the owner."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:60
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The deterministic rule (electHolder): the active session that owns the P0 PR, else the earliest-created active session, the session id breaking a tie. Stalled sessions are not candidates. Every sibling computes the same answer from the same listing (owner ruling, 2026-11-07)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:102
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The elected session holds the merge steward lane and runs its loop until it hands over or the lane lapses."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The measured condition (laneNeeded): two or more active sessions have ready PRs in the same repositories, and either the runners are contended (more than about 10 queued runs on a repository, or the oldest queued run older than about 30 minutes) or PRs conflict with or supersede each other (owner ruling, 2026-11-07)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The merge manager owns the landing from here: it reports landed, or hands the PR back with the reason."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:16
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The sibling's side of merging (owner ruling, 2026-11-07). A coding agent with a PR ready to merge does not know whether a merge manager exists, so it checks: if one is active and live, it sends the six-line merge request; if none is, it measures whether one is needed, and either runs the merge manager loop for its own PRs or elects one with its siblings by the fixed rule, the winner announcing itself to all and taking the lane. Any agent may stall, the merge manager included: a request not acknowledged within the stall window sends the sibling to stalled-agent triage and a re-election without the stalled session. The merge manager's own loop is Process_MergeManagerWatch."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:79
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "To the merge manager: the PR URL and full head SHA, the session URL, 1-3 sentences on the change, the rendered preview URL or no preview with a reason, what to look for, and full tier green as judged (owner ruling, 2026-11-07). Never merge it yourself, and never push to another session's branch."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:97
#. Diagram label
msgid "With the merge manager"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:113
#. Diagram label
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:41
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when the latest \"merge manager: <session id>\" announcement in the coordination group names a session that is live: active, and it answered within the stall window (holding.stalledAfterMinutes). The announcement is sent to every sibling and the owner, and noted durably on the coordination work item, so a newly started sibling finds it. No when there is no announcement, the holder handed over or lapsed, or the holder is stalled."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when the merge manager acknowledged the request within the stall window. No when it did not, or its session went inactive: the lane is treated as vacant."
msgstr ""
